<title>ESTONIA: ESTONIA-RADIO HEADLINES EARLY AFTERNOON.</title>
<headline>ESTONIA-RADIO HEADLINES EARLY AFTERNOON.</headline>
<dateline>TALLINN 1997-03-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>These were the headlines on Estonian Kuku radio in the early afternoon:</p>
<p>- Tartu 2000, the Coalition Party faction in Tartu, has not yet decided if it will join the Reform Party in Thursday's vote of no-confidence against mayor Tonis Lukas.</p>
<p>- The miners union has accepted the need for cutbacks in the mine industry but has suggested that young workers be kept on. The Oil Shale company wants to cut 10 percent of the workforce or 900 jobs.</p>
<p>-- Tallinn Newsroom +372 630 8400</p>
</text>
